lt1\sb1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li359\ri4504\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Accelerating dynamometer tests, where the engine speed is constantly\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 increasing (i.e. 300 RPM/sec), can under-estimate an engine's steady state performance.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 You may think an accelerating test best represents an\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 engine\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 accelerating\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 in\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 a\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 vehicle.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 However,\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Drag\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Racing\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Analyzer\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 calculates\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 power\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 loss\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 due\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 to accelerating the engine, which changes in each gear.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 See "Inertia" discussion in this Appendix.\par\sect\sectd\sbkpage\headery365\footery413\lndscpsxn\margtsxn740\margbsxn600\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb253\f0\fs28\b0\i0\par
